meta {
  name: replace current user
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

put {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/user/
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessTokenStudent}}
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required on a PUT -- omitting a field blanks it.
    "username": "marco.reyes@example.com",
    "first_name": "Marco",
    "last_name": "Reyes"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Full replacement of the Django `User` record. Prefer `PATCH` -- see
  **update current user** -- since anything omitted here is blanked.

  `username` is the account's email in this project (registration and checkout
  both set it that way), so changing it detaches the login from the email. There
  is almost never a reason to send it.

  Again: this is the auth record, not the student profile. Name, country,
  timezone and Spanish level live on `PATCH /student/me/`.

  ## API example response
  {
    "pk": 4,
    "username": "marco.reyes@example.com",
    "email": "marco.reyes@example.com",
    "first_name": "Marco",
    "last_name": "Reyes"
  }
}
